{
  "an6.37:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.37 ",
  "an6.37:0.2": "4. Deities ",
  "an6.37:0.3": "A Gift With Six Factors ",
  "an6.37:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an6.37:1.2": "Now at that time Veḷukaṇṭakī, Nanda’s mother, was preparing a religious donation with six factors for the mendicant Saṅgha headed by Sāriputta and Moggallāna. ",
  "an6.37:1.3": "The Buddha saw her doing this, with his clairvoyance that is purified and superhuman, ",
  "an6.37:1.4": "and he addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an6.37:1.5": "“This Veḷukaṇṭakī, Nanda’s mother, is preparing a religious donation with six factors for the mendicant Saṅgha headed by Sāriputta and Moggallāna. ",
  "an6.37:2.1": "And how does a religious donation have six factors? ",
  "an6.37:2.2": "Three factors apply to the donor and three to the recipients. ",
  "an6.37:2.3": "What three factors apply to the donor? ",
  "an6.37:2.4": "It’s when a donor is in a good mood before giving, while giving they feel confident, and after giving they’re uplifted. ",
  "an6.37:2.5": "These three factors apply to the donor. ",
  "an6.37:3.1": "What three factors apply to the recipients? ",
  "an6.37:3.2": "It’s when the recipients are free of greed, hate, and delusion, or practicing to be free of them. ",
  "an6.37:3.3": "These three factors apply to the recipients. ",
  "an6.37:3.4": "Thus three factors apply to the donor and three to the recipients. ",
  "a